cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software in your research, please cite both the method paper
  and the software itself.
title: didc
abstract: >-
  Difference-in-discontinuities estimation, validity testing and partial
  identification for Stata. In a regression-discontinuity design where a
  confounding policy is assigned by the same cutoff as the treatment of
  interest, the continuity assumption underlying standard RD fails; didc
  recovers the effect from the change in the outcome over time at the cutoff,
  and provides the two validity tests and the bounded-variation bounds of
  Picchetti, Pinto & Shinoki (2026).
